        "original_id": "234c25e1-28bb-56fc-b91a-5d219ca98275",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James Kerwin, Paul Verhoeven, Chase Masterson, Kipleigh Brown, John Newton, Mik Scriba\n- Places: St. Louis, Missouri\n- Works: Yesterday Was a Lie, Burned with Desire\n- Roles: film director, theatre director, film producer, television director, television producer, screenwriter, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Verhoeven was born on 18 July 1938 and is a Dutch film director, film producer, television director, television producer, and screenwriter.\n- James Kerwin was born on October 13, 1973, in St. Louis, Missouri, and is an American film and theatre director.\n- Yesterday Was a Lie is a 2008 neo-noir film written and directed by James Kerwin.\n- Yesterday Was a Lie stars Kipleigh Brown, Chase Masterson, John Newton, and Mik Scriba.\n- Chase Masterson performed a cover of Burned with Desire for an early cut of Yesterday Was a Lie.\n- Chase Masterson's cover of Burned with Desire was not included in the commercial release of Yesterday Was a Lie.",
